Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the tt-metal repository license).

This directory vendors code and designs from two Apache-2.0 sources.

1. Cloudflare/clef release code
   Source:  https://huggingface.co/Cloudflare/clef, file joint_schema_model.py
   Revision: 2f3de3dd85f379784083b0814d997ab627200f0c
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (the LICENSE file of that repository)
   Vendored:
     tt/head.py  <- joint_schema_model.py lines 242 to 461: the classes EvidenceRoutingLayer and
                    JointSchemaHead, copied verbatim so the joint schema head runs on the host CPU
                    in fp32 without loading the release backbone.
   Used at run time without copying (loaded from the weights snapshot with importlib):
     encode_record, render, question_options, systemone_answer, SYSTEM_PROMPT and the token
     helpers of joint_schema_model.py (tt/encode.py, tt/server.py).

2. kev (jaredpalmer/kev) serving design, through the Tenstorrent kev-9b port
   Source:  https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev at commit 952ce9d, and
            models/autoports/jaredpalmer_kev_9b in this repository (its NOTICE lists kev's files)
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0
   Reused as a design and partly as code (rewritten for Clef's joint head, no byte copies of kev):
     tt/server.py  <- jaredpalmer_kev_9b/tt/server.py: Settings, parse_mesh_shape, worker threads,
                      least-recently-used prefix cache with per-slot handling, the FastAPI routes
                      and middleware, the lifespan, the request log line.
     tt/api.py     <- jaredpalmer_kev_9b/tt/api.py: request model layout. The validation rules and
                      the answer bodies follow joint_schema_model.systemone() instead of kev.
     tt/fake_engine.py <- the FakeEngine of jaredpalmer_kev_9b/tt/server.py (seeded pseudo-random
                      hidden rows through the real head and tokenizer).
     tests/test_server_api.py <- jaredpalmer_kev_9b/tests/test_server_api.py (test plan).
   Demo presets (demo/presets.json, when the demo stage ships them) reuse kev's Apache-2.0 presets
   and labelled development records as jaredpalmer_kev_9b/NOTICE describes.

The vendored code was reduced to what the Tenstorrent serving path needs. Class and function
names of the Cloudflare release are unchanged.

